# Pawse Web（前端）

宠物不舒服时，**打给 Pawse 说说**。以语音为主，需要时再开摄像头或发照片。
Pawse 用语音回答、给出分级和下一步建议，然后先列出附近的诊所，选好后**帮你打给兽医**，也可以**帮你问保险**。

```
首页 → 语音通话（摄像头 / 照片 / 文字 / 关键词都是可选）→ 建议卡
     → 转接兽医：先看附近诊所列表 → 选一家 → Pawse 打过去（德语 + 实时翻译）
     → 转接保险：Pawse 打给保险公司
     → 总结页
```

默认是**演示模式**：对话、诊所、电话都是脚本数据，Pawse 用浏览器自带的声音读出来（电话里读德语）。
队友的三个工具放到 GitHub 后，替换下面三个“插槽”文件就能接上，可以一个一个接。

## 快速开始

```bash
npm install
npm run dev        # 浏览器打开 localhost:5173
npm run check      # 纯 Node 检查演示数据、接口契约和金额（不需要装依赖）
```

- 想演快一点：`localhost:5173/?speed=3`（倍速时不出声，只走字幕）。
- 演示里你不说话的话，几秒后 Pawse 会“听到”脚本里的回答；点关键词或打字会马上用你的输入。
- 摄像头 / 麦克风 / 定位：电脑上 `localhost` 可以直接用。手机用局域网 `http://` 打开时浏览器会拦住，需要 HTTPS（部署后就好）。打不开时界面会提示，通话照样能继续。

## 界面

| 页面 | 文件 | 内容 |
|---|---|---|
| 首页 | `src/pages/Home.jsx` | 虚拟形象 Pawse、“呼叫 Pawse” |
| 语音通话 | `src/pages/VoiceCall.jsx` | 大头像（说话时嘴会动、有光圈）；字幕；关键词；文字框 + 📷 发照片；麦克风 / 挂断 / 摄像头（可选，打开后变成小画面）；分诊后弹出建议卡 |
| 诊所列表 | `src/pages/ClinicList.jsx` | 按距离排序；营业中 / 已关门 / 急诊 / 最近；地图链接；“让 Pawse 打” |
| 转接电话 | `src/pages/PhoneCall.jsx` | 呼叫中 → 通话中；原话（德语）+ 实时翻译；结果卡 |
| 总结 | `src/pages/Plan.jsx` | 建议、已完成的电话、可复制的病情摘要、理赔材料 |

虚拟形象在 `src/components/Avatar.jsx`，颜色在 `src/styles.css` 顶部的 `:root`。

## 插槽一：语音智能体（给语音队友）

替换 `src/agents/liveVoiceAgent.js`，导出 `createLiveVoiceAgent({ lang })`：

```js
agent.on(cb)                          // 订阅事件，返回取消订阅函数
agent.start()
agent.end()                           // 必须发出一次 {type:'ended'}
agent.sendText(text)                  // 用户打字，或点了关键词
agent.sendImage(file)                 // 用户拍 / 选的照片（可选功能）
agent.attachMedia({ audio, video })   // 麦克风 MediaStream；video 只有用户打开摄像头时才有，否则 null
agent.setMicMuted(bool)
agent.wantsAudio = true               // 页面会打开麦克风
```

要发出的事件：

```js
{ type: 'transcript', role: 'user' | 'ai', text }     // 字幕
{ type: 'speaking', who: 'user' | 'ai' | 'none' }     // 控制形象的嘴和光圈
{ type: 'listening', on: true | false }               // “在听…”
{ type: 'suggestions', items: ['瘸腿', '呕吐', …] }    // 关键词（[] 隐藏）
{ type: 'image_received' }                            // 收到照片
{ type: 'triage', level: 'red'|'yellow'|'green', headline, steps: [...], escalation, summary }
{ type: 'error', message }
{ type: 'ended' }
```

AI 的声音由智能体自己播放。

## 插槽二：诊所搜索 / 地图（给搜索队友）

替换 `src/agents/liveClinicSearch.js`，导出：

```js
liveSearchClinics({ lang, location, triage })  →  Promise<{ clinics: [...] }>
```

- `location`：`{ lat, lng }`；用户不给定位时是 `null`（页面会提示“距离可能不准”）
- `triage`：Pawse 的判断，比如 `level === 'red'` 时可以优先急诊

每家诊所：

```js
{ id, name, address, distanceKm: 0.8, openNow: true,
  hoursText: '营业到 18:30', emergency: false, rating: 4.7, mapsUrl: 'https://…' }
```

页面按你返回的顺序显示；已关门的诊所不能点“让 Pawse 打”。用户选中的诊所会作为 `context.clinic` 传给插槽三。

## 插槽三：打电话智能体（给电话队友）

替换 `src/agents/livePhoneAgent.js`，导出 `createLivePhoneCall({ target, lang, context })`：

- `target`：`'vet'` 或 `'insurance'`
- `context`：`{ summary, clinic, estimate }`，分别是病情摘要、用户选的诊所（含名字和地址，电话号码可以由插槽二一起给），以及打保险时兽医给的预估价

```js
call.on(cb); call.start(); call.hangup();
```

要发出的事件：

```js
{ type: 'status', state: 'dialing' | 'connected' | 'ended' }
{ type: 'speaking', who: 'ai' | 'callee' | 'none' }
{ type: 'line', who: 'ai' | 'callee', original: '德语原话', text: '翻译' }
{ type: 'result', kind: 'appointment', time: '16:30', place, estimate: 600, currency: 'CHF', note }     // 兽医
{ type: 'result', kind: 'coverage', covered, currency, deductible, rate, estimate,
  reimbursed, outOfPocket, points: [{ ok, text, ref }] }                                            // 保险
{ type: 'error', message }
```

约定：**每通电话的第一句先说明“我是 AI 助手，代表主人来电”**。

## 切换到真实工具

在 `.env.local` 里（参考 `.env.example`），三块可以分开切：

```
VITE_VOICE_AGENT=live
VITE_VOICE_AGENT_URL=wss://…
VITE_CLINIC_SEARCH=live
VITE_CLINIC_SEARCH_URL=https://…
VITE_PHONE_AGENT=live
VITE_PHONE_AGENT_URL=wss://…
```

插槽里默认写了最简单的连接方式（语音和电话用 WebSocket，搜索用 POST）。服务端直接按上面的格式返回就能用，不一样的话改插槽文件就行。
完整定义在 `src/contracts.js`。数据格式不对时，浏览器控制台会出现 `[Pawse]` 警告，方便联调。

## 目录

```
src/
  App.jsx                 页面切换：home → voice → clinics → phone → plan
  contracts.js            三个工具的接口 + 校验
  config.js               环境开关、?speed=
  i18n.js                 中英文文案
  styles.css              樱花粉主题
  pages/                  Home / VoiceCall / ClinicList / PhoneCall / Plan
  components/             Avatar（虚拟形象）/ Icon / PlanPanel（建议卡）
  hooks/useUserMedia.js   打开麦克风 / 摄像头
  agents/
    index.js              按环境变量选演示版或真实版
    mockVoiceAgent.js     演示：语音对话
    mockClinicSearch.js   演示：诊所列表（虚构诊所，名字带 “(Demo)”）
    mockPhoneAgent.js     演示：打电话
    mockScripts.js        演示台词（中英文 + 德语）、诊所、金额
    speech.js             演示用的浏览器语音
    liveVoiceAgent.js     ← 插槽一：语音队友
    liveClinicSearch.js   ← 插槽二：搜索队友
    livePhoneAgent.js     ← 插槽三：电话队友
  utils/                  病情摘要、复制
scripts/check-agents.mjs  纯 Node 检查
```

## 注意

- 演示台词、诊所和金额都是**占位内容**，不是兽医或保险建议，诊所是虚构的。德语请找会德语的人看一眼。
- 演示里的电话是脚本，没有真的打出去。真的外呼要先让用户确认，并符合当地的录音和 AI 来电规定。
{
  "name": "pet-triage-web",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "private": true,
  "type": "module",
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "vite --host",
    "build": "vite build",
    "preview": "vite preview --host",
    "check": "node scripts/check-agents.mjs"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "react": "^19.2.0",
    "react-dom": "^19.2.0"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@vitejs/plugin-react": "^5.0.0",
    "vite": "^7.0.0"
  }
}
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import react from '@vitejs/plugin-react';

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()],
  server: { port: 5173 },
});
# Copy to .env.local and edit. Defaults run everything on the scripted demo.
# Each part can be switched on its own.

# 1. Voice conversation with Pawse (camera / photos optional): mock | live
VITE_VOICE_AGENT=mock
VITE_VOICE_AGENT_URL=

# 2. Finding nearby vet clinics before calling: mock | live
VITE_CLINIC_SEARCH=mock
VITE_CLINIC_SEARCH_URL=

# 3. Pawse calling the vet / the insurer: mock | live
VITE_PHONE_AGENT=mock
VITE_PHONE_AGENT_URL=
// Central switches. Set them in .env.local (see .env.example).
// import.meta.env is undefined outside Vite (e.g. plain-Node checks), so guard it.
const env = (typeof import.meta !== 'undefined' && import.meta.env) || {};

/** 'mock' = scripted demo (default). 'live' = the teammate's agent. */
export const VOICE_AGENT = env.VITE_VOICE_AGENT || 'mock';
export const CLINIC_SEARCH = env.VITE_CLINIC_SEARCH || 'mock';
export const PHONE_AGENT = env.VITE_PHONE_AGENT || 'mock';

export const VOICE_AGENT_URL = env.VITE_VOICE_AGENT_URL || '';
export const CLINIC_SEARCH_URL = env.VITE_CLINIC_SEARCH_URL || '';
export const PHONE_AGENT_URL = env.VITE_PHONE_AGENT_URL || '';

/** Mock playback speed. "?speed=3" in the URL plays the demo 3x faster (handy for rehearsing). */
export const MOCK_SPEED = (() => {
  try {
    const v = Number(new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('speed'));
    return v > 0 ? v : 1;
  } catch {
    return 1;
  }
})();
// The interfaces between this frontend and the teammates' agents.
// Keep this file the single source of truth; README.md mirrors it.

/**
 * ============================================================ 1. VOICE AGENT
 * Voice conversation between the user and Pawse. Camera and photos are optional extras.
 * Teammate replaces src/agents/liveVoiceAgent.js.
 *
 * createVoiceAgent({ lang }) returns:
 *   on(cb) -> unsubscribe
 *   start()
 *   end()                          must emit {type:'ended'} exactly once
 *   sendText(text)                 typed text, or a tapped keyword chip
 *   sendImage(file)                a photo the user took or picked (File / Blob)
 *   attachMedia({ audio, video })  MediaStreams from the page; either may be null
 *                                  (audio = mic when wantsAudio; video = only while the camera is on)
 *   setMicMuted(bool)
 *   wantsAudio: boolean            if true the page opens the microphone
 *
 * Events:
 *   {type:'transcript', role:'user'|'ai', text, simulated?}   live captions
 *   {type:'speaking', who:'user'|'ai'|'none'}                  drives the avatar
 *   {type:'listening', on:boolean}
 *   {type:'suggestions', items:string[]}                       keyword chips ([] hides them)
 *   {type:'image_received'}                                    the last photo arrived
 *   {type:'triage', level, headline, steps:string[], escalation?:string, summary:string}
 *   {type:'error', message}
 *   {type:'ended'}
 *
 * ============================================================ 2. CLINIC SEARCH
 * Finds nearby vet clinics, shown as a list before Pawse calls one.
 * Teammate replaces src/agents/liveClinicSearch.js.
 *
 * searchClinics({ lang, location, triage }) -> Promise<{ clinics: Clinic[] }>
 *   location = { lat, lng } or null (user refused / unavailable)
 *
 * Clinic = { id, name, address, distanceKm, openNow:boolean, hoursText?, emergency?:boolean,
 *            rating?:number, mapsUrl? }
 *
 * ============================================================ 3. PHONE AGENT
 * Pawse calls the chosen clinic or the insurer for the user.
 * Teammate replaces src/agents/livePhoneAgent.js.
 *
 * createPhoneCall({ target:'vet'|'insurance', lang, context }) returns:
 *   on(cb) -> unsubscribe
 *   start()
 *   hangup()
 *   context = { summary: string, clinic?: Clinic, estimate?: number }
 *
 * Events:
 *   {type:'status', state:'dialing'|'connected'|'ended'}
 *   {type:'speaking', who:'ai'|'callee'|'none'}
 *   {type:'line', who:'ai'|'callee', original:string, text:string}   original language + translation
 *   {type:'result', ...}
 *   {type:'error', message}
 *
 * result for 'vet':       {kind:'appointment', time, place, estimate:number, currency, note?}
 * result for 'insurance': {kind:'coverage', covered, currency, deductible, rate, estimate,
 *                          reimbursed, outOfPocket, points:[{ok, text, ref?}]}
 */

export const LEVELS = ['red', 'yellow', 'green'];

/** Problems with a triage event (empty list = OK). */
export function validateTriage(e) {
  const p = [];
  if (!e || typeof e !== 'object') return ['triage is not an object'];
  if (!LEVELS.includes(e.level)) p.push(`level must be one of ${LEVELS.join('|')}`);
  if (!e.headline) p.push('headline missing');
  if (!Array.isArray(e.steps) || !e.steps.length) p.push('steps must be a non-empty array');
  if (typeof e.summary !== 'string' || !e.summary) p.push('summary missing');
  return p;
}

/** Problems with a clinic list (empty list = OK). */
export function validateClinics(res) {
  const p = [];
  if (!res || !Array.isArray(res.clinics)) return ['expected { clinics: [...] }'];
  res.clinics.forEach((c, i) => {
    if (!c.id) p.push(`clinics[${i}].id missing`);
    if (!c.name) p.push(`clinics[${i}].name missing`);
    if (typeof c.distanceKm !== 'number') p.push(`clinics[${i}].distanceKm must be a number`);
    if (typeof c.openNow !== 'boolean') p.push(`clinics[${i}].openNow must be true/false`);
  });
  return p;
}

/** Problems with a phone-call result (empty list = OK). */
export function validateResult(target, r) {
  const p = [];
  if (!r || typeof r !== 'object') return ['result is not an object'];
  if (target === 'vet') {
    if (r.kind !== 'appointment') p.push("vet result kind must be 'appointment'");
    if (!r.time) p.push('time missing');
    if (typeof r.estimate !== 'number') p.push('estimate must be a number');
  } else if (target === 'insurance') {
    if (r.kind !== 'coverage') p.push("insurance result kind must be 'coverage'");
    for (const k of ['deductible', 'rate', 'estimate', 'reimbursed', 'outOfPocket']) {
      if (typeof r[k] !== 'number') p.push(`${k} must be a number`);
    }
    if (!Array.isArray(r.points)) p.push('points must be an array');
  } else p.push(`unknown target ${target}`);
  return p;
}
import { VOICE_AGENT, CLINIC_SEARCH, PHONE_AGENT, MOCK_SPEED } from '../config.js';
import { createMockVoiceAgent } from './mockVoiceAgent.js';
import { createLiveVoiceAgent } from './liveVoiceAgent.js';
import { mockSearchClinics } from './mockClinicSearch.js';
import { liveSearchClinics } from './liveClinicSearch.js';
import { createMockPhoneCall } from './mockPhoneAgent.js';
import { createLivePhoneCall } from './livePhoneAgent.js';

export const IS_LIVE_VOICE = VOICE_AGENT === 'live';
export const IS_LIVE_CLINICS = CLINIC_SEARCH === 'live';
export const IS_LIVE_PHONE = PHONE_AGENT === 'live';
export const IS_MOCK = !IS_LIVE_VOICE || !IS_LIVE_CLINICS || !IS_LIVE_PHONE;

/** The page opens the microphone only if the active voice agent wants audio. */
export const VOICE_WANTS_AUDIO = IS_LIVE_VOICE;

/** 1. Voice conversation with Pawse. */
export function createVoiceAgent(opts) {
  return IS_LIVE_VOICE ? createLiveVoiceAgent(opts) : createMockVoiceAgent({ speed: MOCK_SPEED, ...opts });
}

/** 2. Nearby vet clinics. */
export function searchClinics(opts) {
  return IS_LIVE_CLINICS ? liveSearchClinics(opts) : mockSearchClinics({ speed: MOCK_SPEED, ...opts });
}

/** 3. Pawse calls the clinic or the insurer. */
export function createPhoneCall(opts) {
  return IS_LIVE_PHONE ? createLivePhoneCall(opts) : createMockPhoneCall({ speed: MOCK_SPEED, ...opts });
}
// SLOT 2 – FOR THE CLINIC-SEARCH (MAP) TEAMMATE.
//
// Replace this file with the real search from your repo (or import it from there).
// It must export searchClinics({ lang, location, triage }) and resolve to
//
//   { clinics: [ { id, name, address, distanceKm, openNow, hoursText?, emergency?, rating?, mapsUrl? } ] }
//
// `location` is { lat, lng } when the user allowed it, otherwise null.
// `triage` is Pawse's verdict ({ level, headline, summary, … }) – useful to prefer emergency
// clinics when level === 'red'. The page shows the list in the order you return it.
//
// Switch on with VITE_CLINIC_SEARCH=live and VITE_CLINIC_SEARCH_URL=https://… in .env.local.

import { CLINIC_SEARCH_URL } from '../config.js';

export async function liveSearchClinics({ lang = 'zh', location = null, triage = null } = {}) {
  if (!CLINIC_SEARCH_URL) throw new Error('VITE_CLINIC_SEARCH_URL is not set: clinic search is not connected yet.');
  const res = await fetch(CLINIC_SEARCH_URL, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ lang, location, level: triage && triage.level, summary: triage && triage.summary }),
  });
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`Clinic search failed (${res.status})`);
  return res.json();
}
// SLOT FOR THE PHONE-CALL TEAMMATE.
//
// Replace this file with the real calling agent from your repo (or import it from there).
// It must return the PHONE AGENT shape documented in ../contracts.js:
//
//   on(cb) / start() / hangup()
//
// and emit: status, speaking, line {who, original, text}, result, error.
// `context.summary` is the case summary Pawse should pass on; `context.estimate` is the
// vet's price estimate once the vet call has happened (useful for the insurer call).
//
// Switch on with VITE_PHONE_AGENT=live and VITE_PHONE_AGENT_URL=wss://… in .env.local.

import { PHONE_AGENT_URL } from '../config.js';

export function createLivePhoneCall({ target = 'vet', lang = 'zh', context = {} } = {}) {
  const listeners = new Set();
  const emit = (e) => listeners.forEach((l) => l(e));
  let ws = null;
  let ended = false;

  return {
    on(cb) {
      listeners.add(cb);
      return () => listeners.delete(cb);
    },
    start() {
      if (!PHONE_AGENT_URL) {
        emit({ type: 'error', message: 'VITE_PHONE_AGENT_URL is not set: the live phone agent is not connected yet.' });
        emit({ type: 'status', state: 'ended' });
        return;
      }
      emit({ type: 'status', state: 'dialing' });
      ws = new WebSocket(PHONE_AGENT_URL);
      ws.onopen = () => ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'start_call', target, lang, context }));
      ws.onmessage = (msg) => {
        try {
          emit(JSON.parse(msg.data));
        } catch {
          /* ignore non-JSON frames */
        }
      };
      ws.onerror = () => emit({ type: 'error', message: 'Phone agent connection failed.' });
    },
    hangup() {
      if (ended) return;
      ended = true;
      try {
        if (ws && ws.readyState === 1) ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'hangup' }));
        ws && ws.close();
      } catch {
        /* ignore */
      }
      emit({ type: 'status', state: 'ended' });
    },
  };
}
// SLOT 1 – FOR THE VOICE TEAMMATE.
//
// Replace this file with the real agent from your repo (or import it from there).
// It must return the VOICE AGENT shape documented in ../contracts.js:
//
//   on(cb) / start() / end() / sendText(text) / sendImage(file)
//   attachMedia({ audio, video }) / setMicMuted(bool) / wantsAudio
//
// and emit: transcript, speaking, listening, suggestions, image_received, triage, error, ended.
//
// Voice is the main channel: the page opens the microphone (wantsAudio = true) and passes it
// as `audio`. The camera is optional – `video` is a MediaStream only while the user has it on,
// otherwise null. Photos arrive through sendImage(file). Play the AI's audio yourself.
//
// Switch on with VITE_VOICE_AGENT=live and VITE_VOICE_AGENT_URL=wss://… in .env.local.

import { VOICE_AGENT_URL } from '../config.js';

export function createLiveVoiceAgent({ lang = 'zh' } = {}) {
  const listeners = new Set();
  const emit = (e) => listeners.forEach((l) => l(e));
  let ws = null;
  let ended = false;

  const send = (obj) => {
    if (ws && ws.readyState === 1) ws.send(JSON.stringify(obj));
  };

  return {
    wantsAudio: true,
    on(cb) {
      listeners.add(cb);
      return () => listeners.delete(cb);
    },
    start() {
      if (!VOICE_AGENT_URL) {
        emit({ type: 'error', message: 'VITE_VOICE_AGENT_URL is not set: the live voice agent is not connected yet.' });
        return;
      }
      ws = new WebSocket(`${VOICE_AGENT_URL}?lang=${encodeURIComponent(lang)}`);
      ws.onmessage = (msg) => {
        try {
          emit(JSON.parse(msg.data)); // enough if the server already speaks the contract
        } catch {
          /* binary frames (audio) – TODO(teammate): play them */
        }
      };
      ws.onerror = () => emit({ type: 'error', message: 'Voice agent connection failed.' });
    },
    end() {
      if (ended) return;
      ended = true;
      try {
        ws && ws.close();
      } catch {
        /* ignore */
      }
      emit({ type: 'ended' });
    },
    sendText(text) {
      send({ type: 'user_text', text });
    },
    sendImage(file) {
      // Simple default: send the photo as a data URL. Change to an upload if you prefer.
      const reader = new FileReader();
      reader.onload = () => send({ type: 'user_image', dataUrl: reader.result });
      reader.readAsDataURL(file);
    },
    attachMedia(/* { audio, video } */) {
      // TODO(teammate): stream mic audio (and camera frames while video != null) to the model.
    },
    setMicMuted(/* muted */) {
      // TODO(teammate): pause / resume sending mic audio.
    },
  };
}
// Plain-Node checks for the mock agents and the contracts. Run with: npm run check

import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { createMockVoiceAgent } from '../src/agents/mockVoiceAgent.js';
import { mockSearchClinics } from '../src/agents/mockClinicSearch.js';
import { createMockPhoneCall } from '../src/agents/mockPhoneAgent.js';
import { reimbursement } from '../src/agents/mockScripts.js';
import { validateTriage, validateResult, validateClinics } from '../src/contracts.js';
import { buildSummary } from '../src/utils/summary.js';

const SPEED = 400;
let n = 0;
const ok = (m) => console.log(`  ok  ${++n} ${m}`);

function runVideo({ lang, onEvent, stopOn } = {}) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const events = [];
    const a = createMockVoiceAgent({ lang, speed: SPEED });
    const to = setTimeout(() => reject(new Error('video timeout')), 5000);
    a.on((e) => {
      events.push(e);
      onEvent && onEvent(e, a);
      if (e.type === 'triage' || (stopOn && stopOn(e))) {
        clearTimeout(to);
        setTimeout(() => {
          a.end();
          setTimeout(() => resolve({ events, a }), 30);
        }, 20);
      }
    });
    a.start();
  });
}

function runPhone(target, lang, context) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const events = [];
    const c = createMockPhoneCall({ target, lang, context, speed: SPEED });
    const to = setTimeout(() => reject(new Error('phone timeout')), 5000);
    c.on((e) => {
      events.push(e);
      if (e.type === 'status' && e.state === 'ended') {
        clearTimeout(to);
        setTimeout(() => resolve({ events, c }), 30);
      }
    });
    c.start();
  });
}

for (const lang of ['zh', 'en']) {
  console.log(`voice agent (${lang})`);

  // nobody answers: the mock "hears" scripted answers and reaches triage
  const auto = await runVideo({ lang });
  const tri = auto.events.find((e) => e.type === 'triage');
  assert.deepEqual(validateTriage(tri), []);
  assert.equal(tri.level, 'yellow');
  ok('reaches a valid triage with no input (simulated answers)');

  const firstAi = auto.events.find((e) => e.type === 'transcript');
  assert.equal(firstAi.role, 'ai');
  ok('Pawse speaks first');

  const users = auto.events.filter((e) => e.type === 'transcript' && e.role === 'user');
  assert.equal(users.length, 2);
  assert.ok(users.every((u) => u.simulated === true));
  ok('two simulated user answers, flagged simulated');

  const sug = auto.events.filter((e) => e.type === 'suggestions');
  assert.ok(sug[0].items.length >= 3, 'keyword chips offered');
  assert.deepEqual(sug[1].items, [], 'chips cleared after answering');
  ok('keyword chips appear while listening and clear after the answer');

  assert.equal(auto.events.filter((e) => e.type === 'ended').length, 1);
  auto.a.end();
  assert.equal(auto.events.filter((e) => e.type === 'ended').length, 1);
  ok('end() emits ended once and is idempotent');

  // the user taps a chip / types: their words are used, not the script
  const typed = await runVideo({
    lang,
    onEvent: (e, a) => {
      if (e.type === 'suggestions' && e.items.length) queueMicrotask(() => a.sendText(e.items[0]));
    },
  });
  const typedUsers = typed.events.filter((e) => e.type === 'transcript' && e.role === 'user');
  assert.equal(typedUsers.length, 2);
  assert.ok(typedUsers.every((u) => u.simulated === false));
  ok('tapping a keyword answers immediately with that keyword');

  // hanging up mid-conversation stops everything
  const early = await runVideo({ lang, stopOn: (e) => e.type === 'listening' && e.on });
  assert.ok(!early.events.some((e) => e.type === 'triage'));
  assert.equal(early.events[early.events.length - 1].type, 'ended');
  ok('hang-up while listening stops cleanly, nothing after ended');

  // photo while listening: acknowledged once, conversation still reaches triage
  const withPhoto = await runVideo({
    lang,
    onEvent: (e, a) => {
      if (e.type === 'listening' && e.on) queueMicrotask(() => { a.sendImage({ name: 'cat.jpg' }); a.sendImage({ name: 'cat2.jpg' }); });
    },
  });
  assert.equal(withPhoto.events.filter((e) => e.type === 'image_received').length, 4);
  const thanks = withPhoto.events.filter((e) => e.type === 'transcript' && e.role === 'ai' && /Got the photo|收到照片/.test(e.text));
  assert.equal(thanks.length, 1);
  assert.ok(withPhoto.events.some((e) => e.type === 'triage'));
  ok('photos: each one acknowledged with image_received, thanked once, triage still reached');

  console.log(`clinic search (${lang})`);
  const found = await mockSearchClinics({ lang, speed: SPEED });
  assert.deepEqual(validateClinics(found), []);
  const d = found.clinics.map((c) => c.distanceKm);
  assert.deepEqual(d, [...d].sort((x, y) => x - y));
  assert.ok(found.clinics.some((c) => !c.openNow) && found.clinics.some((c) => c.emergency));
  assert.ok(found.clinics.every((c) => typeof c.hoursText === 'string' && c.mapsUrl.startsWith('https://')));
  assert.ok(found.clinics.every((c) => c.name.includes('(Demo)')));
  ok('valid list, sorted by distance, open/closed + emergency, localised hours, demo names');

  console.log(`phone agent (${lang})`);
  const chosen = found.clinics[0];
  const vet = await runPhone('vet', lang, { clinic: chosen });
  const st = vet.events.filter((e) => e.type === 'status').map((e) => e.state);
  assert.deepEqual(st, ['dialing', 'connected', 'ended']);
  ok('vet call: dialing → connected → ended');
  const lines = vet.events.filter((e) => e.type === 'line');
  assert.match(lines[0].original, /KI-Assistent/, 'Pawse must say it is an AI first');
  assert.ok(lines.every((l) => l.original && l.text));
  ok('first line discloses AI; every line has German + translation');
  const vr = vet.events.find((e) => e.type === 'result');
  assert.deepEqual(validateResult('vet', vr), []);
  assert.equal(vr.time, '16:30');
  assert.equal(vr.place, chosen.name);
  ok('vet result: valid appointment at 16:30 at the chosen clinic');

  const ins = await runPhone('insurance', lang, { estimate: vr.estimate });
  const ir = ins.events.find((e) => e.type === 'result');
  assert.deepEqual(validateResult('insurance', ir), []);
  assert.equal(ir.reimbursed, 240);
  assert.equal(ir.outOfPocket, 360);
  assert.ok(ir.points.some((p) => p.ref === 'AVB 1.2.5') && ir.points.some((p) => p.ref === 'AVB 1.2.6'));
  ok('insurance result: 600 → 240 back, 360 out of pocket, AVB clauses listed');

  // hang up while dialing
  const c = createMockPhoneCall({ target: 'vet', lang, speed: SPEED, context: {} });
  const evs = [];
  c.on((e) => evs.push(e));
  c.start();
  c.hangup();
  c.hangup();
  await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 60));
  assert.deepEqual(evs.map((e) => e.state || e.type), ['dialing', 'ended']);
  ok('hang-up while dialing ends once, no result');

  const summary = buildSummary({ lang, triage: tri, vet: vr, insurance: ir });
  assert.ok(summary.includes('16:30') && summary.includes('360') && summary.includes('AVB 1.2.5'));
  ok('case summary includes appointment, out-of-pocket and clauses');
}

console.log('maths');
assert.equal(reimbursement(600), 240);
assert.equal(reimbursement(250), 0);
assert.equal(reimbursement(1000), 560);
ok('reimbursement = 80% above the CHF 300 excess');

